text:
rachel: quick note 4c4 opened PR #531 to fold the structured-output examples into the function/tool calling migration doc: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/531

ben: thanks rachel. quick asks: 1) include a compact validator JSON Schema people can paste, 2) show both named-arg (object) and positional (array) usage, 3) keep a tiny compatibility snippet for older `function_call`.

hugo: agreed on compatibility. also please standardize key name to `tool` (some docs use `toolName` / `tool_id`). call it out once and update examples.

tiago: can we add Ruby and Go parsing snippets? a lot of infra teams use those and we rarely show them in docs.

rachel: adding both. pasting the proposed schema (validator-friendly) below so reviewers can copy/paste. this is intentionally compact and strict.```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool": {"type": "string"},
    "args": {
      "oneOf": [
        {"type": "object"},
        {"type": "array"}
      ]
    },
    "meta": {"type": "object"},
    "confidence": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}
  },
  "required": ["tool", "args"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

ben: nice. can we include a concrete enum example for common tools (web_fetch, cache_get) so validators can be more specific?

hugo: here's a small variant for that:```json
{
  "type":"object",
  "properties":{
    "tool":{"type":"string","enum":["web_fetch","cache_get"]},
    "args":{
      "oneOf":[
        {"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"}},"required":["url"]},
        {"type":"array"}
      ]
    }
  },
  "required":["tool","args"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

tiago: Ruby parsing snippet (minimal) we can add to docs:```ruby
resp = client.generate(prompt: ... )
payload = JSON.parse(resp.output) # payload is a Hash
# symbolize keys if you prefer symbols
payload = payload.transform_keys(&:to_sym) rescue payload
case payload[:tool]
when 'web_fetch'
  fetch(payload[:args]['url'] || payload[:args][0])
end
```

ben: Go example would be useful too. minimal Go runtime snippet:```go
resp := client.Generate(ctx, req)
var payload map[string]interface{}
json.Unmarshal([]byte(resp.Output), &payload)
if payload["tool"] == "web_fetch" {
  args := payload["args"].(map[string]interface{})
  fetch(args["url"].(string))
}
```

hugo: tiny callout: `confidence` is advisory. add a short line: "Do not treat `confidence` as a calibrated probability; validate with your evals or domain rules before automating." link to /guides/evals.

linter-bot: snippet-checker: initial run found an unclosed fence in the Ruby block. patched in branch, re-run CI.

rachel: fixed the fence and pushed. also added a brief compatibility mapping note: "Legacy: map `function_call.name` -> `tool` and `function_call.arguments` -> `args` (object or array)."

ben: i'll do final pass once CI finishes. please ping me if you add more snippets.

rachel: thanks all 680 aiming to merge tomorrow morning if CI is green. appreciate the quick reviews!
